; M1e S1e.2.1 — a built-in predicate below its arity.
;
; `CO-H1`, and the only finding in the review that took the process down: the
; compiler lowered `(eq …)` with no arity check at all, and the check that
; existed was a runtime `assert!` in the matcher whose message — "`eq` needs
; two arguments; ein.py raises IndexError here" — was a parity note rather
; than a diagnostic. `ein saturate` on this file exited **101** with a stack
; trace where every sibling malformation exits 1 with a message.
;
; Why `eq` and not `neq`: the grammar shape-pins `NeqForm`, so `(neq ?x)` is a
; positioned *parse* error and always was. `eq` is an ordinary `GenericList`.
; That is the rule the S1e.1.6 sweep found — four of the seven kernel
; meta-primitives are pinned, and every cell that misbehaves is one of the
; other three.
(relation p T)
(relation q T)

(rule one-armed-guard ()
  :match  (and (p ?x) (eq ?x))
  :assert (q ?x))
